id: pm-o8z748
title: "GH-896: heterogeneous atomic specification batches need batch-local references and one discoverable SDK-first CLI path"
description: "GitHub issue #896 shows that plan materialize applies one shared type and field set to every child. The existing pm item mutate surface already provides heterogeneous atomic create/update/close rows, dry-run, compensation, and resume, but the reported workflow cannot discover it and explicit stable ids prevent an epic plus forward-referencing children from being authored as one coherent specification document."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags[8]: agent-ux,"area:cli","area:sdk",atomic,context-management,github-report,structured-input,token-efficiency
created_at: "2026-08-05T06:02:29.591Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-05T07:05:20.954Z"
closed_at: "2026-08-05T06:43:02.920Z"
completed_at: "2026-08-05T06:43:02.920Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 480
acceptance_criteria: "Public SDK exposes a typed resolver for heterogeneous atomic mutation documents with unique batch-local aliases, stable explicit-or-derived ids, and forward references in parent/dependency fields; pm item mutate accepts the versioned document through its existing stdin path, validates and previews the fully resolved batch before writes, and returns alias-to-id outcomes without adding a competing top-level batch command; CLI, MCP, contracts, completion, SDK docs, errors, token budgets, and 100 percent coverage stay aligned; malformed aliases, cycles, duplicates, unknown references, and replay mismatches fail before tracker mutation; An isolated npm and Bun consumer authors and reads back a mixed Epic/Feature/Decision graph atomically, and a forced mid-batch failure proves compensation leaves no partial active specification"
goal: project management = context management
objective: Make one coherent heterogeneous specification authorable as one atomic SDK-owned mutation document
value: "Agents preserve peak authoring context, avoid orphaned children, and pay one bootstrap instead of one process per item"
impact: Turns the existing atomic mutation substrate into a discoverable universal project-creation primitive without adding a competing command grammar
outcome: "One dry-runnable batch can create mixed item types with per-row metadata and forward references, returning a stable alias-to-id receipt"
why_now: The shipped primitive exists but real users still conclude batching is impossible; the remaining composition and discovery gap is now evidenced by GH-896
parent: pm-mpbb
risk: high
confidence: high
severity: high
environment: "pm CLI 2026.8.4, Node 22/24/26, Linux/macOS/Windows; CLI, public SDK, MCP, completions, contracts, packed npm and Bun consumers"
repro_steps: Create one Plan with multiple steps; pm plan materialize accepts only one materialize type/tags/field set. pm item mutate accepts heterogeneous rows but requires every stable id up front and documents no batch-local forward-reference vocabulary.
resolution: SDK-first batch-local reference resolver shipped with deterministic ids and alias receipts.
expected_result: One atomic document creates and links heterogeneous project context without preallocated ids.
actual_result: "Focused 63-test run, full coverage, and npm/Bun packed acceptance created and read the mixed graph."
customer_impact: "Agents spend one tool call per item, manually correlate ids, and can leave partially authored specifications when a later create fails."
